# Project documentation (agent orientation)

At the **start** of tasks in this workspace, read the relevant map:

- **NAS bridge / container (Node):** `src/PROJECT.md`
- **Windows display client (Python):** `alexa broadcast client/src/PROJECT.md`

These files summarize architecture, data flow, config, UDP protocol v2, tests, and deployment. Use them instead of re-scanning the whole repo when possible.

## Keep docs fresh

When you change **architecture, modules, config keys, Docker/auth workflows, UDP protocol, overlay UI, packaging, or tests**:

1. Update the matching `PROJECT.md` in the **same change** (both if the change spans bridge + client).
2. Bump the **Last updated** date at the top.
3. Add a one-line bullet under **Recent changes** (newest first).

Do not duplicate `README.md` or `DOCKER.md` — those are user guides; `PROJECT.md` is the agent quick-reference.

If unsure whether a change warrants an update, update anyway when behavior or file roles changed.

## Testing (required)

| Suite | Command | Location |
|-------|---------|----------|
| **Full (bridge + client)** | `run_all_tests.bat` | Repo root |
| Bridge only | `npm test` | Repo root — 7 files, Node built-in test runner |
| Client only | `alexa broadcast client\test\run_tests.bat` | Python `unittest` — `test_*.py` |

Bridge tests: `test/*.test.js` — parser, UDP payloads, voice queries, weather location, timer sync.

Client tests: `alexa broadcast client/test/test_*.py` — payload utils, config, weather fetch, main timer routing.

Manual UDP smoke tests: `alexa broadcast client/test/send_test.py --type {broadcast,time,weather,timers,timer-fired}`.

Portable build smoke: after `build_portable.bat`, confirm `dist/alexa-broadcast-client/Run Alexa Broadcast Client.bat` exists and `dist/alexa-broadcast-client-portable.zip` was created.

## Display client packaging (on request only)

Do **not** automatically run `build_portable.bat` after display client edits unless the user explicitly asks to build or ship the portable zip.

When the user **does** ask for a portable build:

1. Run **`alexa broadcast client\build_portable.bat --no-pause`** from a Windows machine with Python 3.10+ (use `subst Z:` if UNC `\\nas\...` breaks `cmd`).
2. **Do not run** `alexa-broadcast-client.exe` or `Run Alexa Broadcast Client.bat` unless the user explicitly asks you to test locally.
3. Confirm outputs exist:
   - `alexa broadcast client/dist/alexa-broadcast-client/Run Alexa Broadcast Client.bat`
   - `alexa broadcast client/dist/alexa-broadcast-client-portable.zip`
4. Tell the user the zip path so they can copy it to the poster PC.

## Commit and push (required workflow)

When the user asks to **commit** and/or **push**:

1. **Run the full test suite first:** `run_all_tests.bat` from repo root (or `npm test` + client `run_tests.bat` sequentially).
2. **Fix all failures** before staging — do not commit with failing tests.
3. **Update `PROJECT.md`** (and this rule if workflow changed) when behavior, tests, or packaging changed.
4. Stage, commit with an accurate message, verify `git status`, then push if requested.

Never skip tests on commit/push requests unless the user explicitly says to.
